    "source_text": "H2O2  (30%  in  H2O;  0.31  mL,  3.0  mmol)  was  added  to  a  stirred  solution  of  1-methylbenzimidazole  1g  (100  mg,  1.0  mmol),  concentrated  H2SO4  (108  μL,  1.0  mmol),  1-Boc-3-(iodo)azetidine  (566  mg,  2.0  mmol)  and  iron(II)  sulfate heptahydrate (80 mg, 0.3 mmol) in DMSO (5 mL) at room temperature. The mixture was stirred at  room  temperature  for  120  min,  then  diluted  with  EtOAc  and  saturated  NaHCO3.  The  aqueous  and  organic  layers  were  partitioned  and  the  organic  layer  was  washed  with  brine,  dried  (MgSO4),  filtered  and  the  solvent  removed  under  vacuum  to  leave  a  crude  residue.  The  residue  was  purified  by  column  chromatography on silica gel using EtOAc / hexanes (3:7 to 7:3) as eluent to give the desired product 3f(52 mg, 17%) as a solid. ",
    "text_sha256": "d81ad70318de38c065efa4fa50b332ef071295a9d464c3d96a220a74a2b42814",
